Subject: base: compose a profile when the launch did not supply one

The loader's only source of a profile is --apostate-profile, so a binary run
with no arguments presents the host. That is the right default for a debug run
and the wrong one for the product: a user who double-clicks the browser expects
a device, not their own machine, and the seed model in docs/FINGERPRINTS.md §5
exists precisely so that launch can be both unique and stable.

This is the one hunk that joins the two halves. The switch still wins, because
it is the strongest layer in §10 and because patch 0005 propagates it to every
child, so a renderer keeps parsing the switch its browser was given and never
composes anything itself. Only when the switch is absent does the browser ask
the compositor, and the compositor returns the same base64 JSON the switch
would have carried — so there is one parser, one format, and one profile
object no matter which path produced it.

ComposeProfileForCurrentProcess() returns nullopt for a child process, for
--fingerprint=host, and when the compiled catalogue cannot serve the launch.
nullopt reaches exactly the code path that already existed, which is host
inheritance.

--- a/base/apostate/profile.cc
+++ b/base/apostate/profile.cc
@@ -7,8 +7,10 @@
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <cmath>
 #include <memory>
+#include <optional>
 #include <utility>
 
+#include "base/apostate/compose.h"
 #include "base/base64.h"
 #include "base/base_switches.h"
 #include "base/command_line.h"
@@ -99,11 +101,31 @@
       return static_cast<const Profile*>(nullptr);
     }
     const CommandLine* command_line = CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess();
-    if (!command_line->HasSwitch(switches::kApostateProfile)) {
+    if (command_line->HasSwitch(::switches::kApostateProfile)) {
+      return static_cast<const Profile*>(ParseOrNull(
+          command_line->GetSwitchValueASCII(::switches::kApostateProfile)));
+    }
+
+    // No switch: compose one. Returns nullopt in a child process, under
+    // --fingerprint=host, and when the catalogue cannot serve this launch;
+    // each of those means inherit the host, which is what the caller below
+    // already does with a null profile.
+    std::optional<std::string> composed = ComposeProfileForCurrentProcess();
+    if (!composed) {
       return static_cast<const Profile*>(nullptr);
     }
-    return static_cast<const Profile*>(ParseOrNull(
-        command_line->GetSwitchValueASCII(switches::kApostateProfile)));
+
+    // Write it back onto this process's command line so the children inherit
+    // it. Patch 0005 propagates --apostate-profile to every child, and a
+    // composed profile that never reaches the renderer is worse than none: the
+    // browser would size its thread pools from the claim while the renderer
+    // reported the host's cores, and navigator.hardwareConcurrency would
+    // contradict the profile. Composition cannot repeat in the child — it is
+    // sandboxed and cannot read the seed file — so the switch is the only
+    // path, and it is the one that already exists.
+    CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess()->AppendSwitchASCII(
+        ::switches::kApostateProfile, *composed);
+    return static_cast<const Profile*>(ParseOrNull(*composed));
   }();
   return profile;
 }
